      "claim": "A related radioligand showed poor brain exposure in cynomolgus monkeys by PET, with total brain uptake reaching only 0.8% of injected dose, arguing against meaningful CNS access for that compound.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "low",
  "decision_summary": "Most direct in-vivo CNS exposure evidence from structurally related molecules supports meaningful BBB penetration after systemic administration, while a minority of poor-exposure records introduces uncertainty; low structural similarity limits confidence.",
